course: dictionary
lesson: 1894
title: Colonial and the history around it
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Colonial comes from colony: a land ruled by another, often faraway, country. The clues help you work out this meaning. «Many objects in European museums were taken from other countries in colonial times.» The sentence says the objects came from other countries, and some people now ask for them back. So colonial times must be a time when one country ruled others.
explain: «Ethiopia... kept its independence through the colonial period, apart from an Italian occupation from 1936 to 1941.» Independence means being free from another country's rule. Ethiopia kept its freedom through the colonial period, which tells you that colonial times were a time when countries could lose their freedom. Put your meaning in the sentence: does it still make sense? Yes.
explain: Colonial can also describe things from that time, like colonial buildings or furniture. Its meaning in science is different: «Colonial animals like coral live joined together in groups.» Always check which meaning fits the sentence around the word.
fact: Colonial means to do with a colony, a land ruled by another, faraway country.
fact: Colonial can describe the time when a country was a colony, such as colonial India.
fact: In the USA, the Colonial period is the time before 1776.
fact: Colonial rule brought trade, but it also brought conquest, unfair treatment and slavery.
fact: Many colonies later fought for independence, which means they wanted to rule themselves.
exercise: «Many objects in European museums were taken from other countries in colonial times.» What does colonial mean here? | About a very old, broken object | About a kind of modern art | *About a time when one country ruled other lands | About a type of museum building
exercise: «Ethiopia... kept its independence through the colonial period.» Find and copy one word that means being free from another country's rule. | *independence | Ethiopia | occupation | capital
exercise: «Colonial animals like coral live joined together in groups.» What does colonial mean in this science sense? | Ruled by a faraway country | Very old and worn | *Living joined together in groups | Found in a museum
test: In the USA, the Colonial period means the time: | *before 1776 | when the USA had no people | only in the summer months | after the year 2000
test: Why do people argue about objects taken in colonial times? | Because colonial objects are always broken | Because the objects are too heavy to move | *Because they were taken unfairly from other countries | Because museums do not have any objects
exam: Which sentence best describes colonial rule in history? | It only affected plants and animals | *It brought trade but also conquest and unfair treatment | It was always fair and kind to everyone | It meant the same as independence
